    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence presents a genuinely balanced picture for AAPL that supports maintaining current positions rather than forcing a directional call. The bull case rests on verified fundamentals \u2014 $39.9B quarterly operating cash flow, a $74.1B equity cushion, and $30.6B in capital returns \u2014 plus genuine technical stabilization with higher lows defending the $165-$167 support zone. The bear case correctly identifies the confirmed downtrend (price below both the 50 SMA at $179.25 and 200 SMA at $181.17 in an active death cross) and fading momentum (MACD histogram decayed 62%, RSI plateaued at 42), but its claims of China weakness, Services deceleration, and regulatory headwinds are unsupported speculation. Critically, the income statement is unavailable, so profitability trends cannot be verified \u2014 a genuine data gap that limits the fundamental case to cash flow alone. Given the competitive evidence on both sides and the unverifiable income statement, Hold is the disciplined call. I will maintain existing positions, hold through the $165-$167 support zone, and set a defined risk line at $165.12 (Bollinger lower band) \u2014 breaking below on rising volume would warrant reducing exposure toward $160 rather than averaging down. I will not add on strength until the stock reclaims the 50 SMA ($179.25) on above-average volume with RSI above 50, which would be the confirmation signal to upgrade.\n\n**Entry Price**: 170.83\n\n**Stop Loss**: 165.12\n\n**Position Sizing**: Keep AAPL at benchmark or slightly below benchmark weight; reserve dry powder for a confirmed breakout above the 50 SMA.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
